<title>GERMANY: Buba's Krupp questions UK suitability for Europe.</title>
<headline>Buba's Krupp questions UK suitability for Europe.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>President of the Hamburg central bank and Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Krupp said on Monday that Britain's &quot;wait-and-see&quot; approach to European economic and monetary union was to be regretted.</p>
<p>Speaking at a meeting organised by the Hamburg savings bank, Krupp said: &quot;It is to be regretted that Britain and Sweden have decided to forego obligatory membership of monetary union.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;In the case of Britain this casts further doubt on the appropriateness of that country being within Europe. As it is legally contentious whether or not a country can be forced to take part in monetary union under EU rules, it will have to follow of its own free will,&quot; said Krupp.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
